From 2c9c5e0784de4ce62baebc1c6e40d23c683ac9a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emscripten-forge <recipes@emscripten-forge>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 00:33:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Complete the interpreter's foreigncall table enough to run
 Base

With JULIACODEGEN=none every ccall goes through the generated table in
src/interpreter-foreigncall.c, and anything it does not cover aborts the
program. Four things were missing:

  * ccall targets written as strings. Parts of Base build the name by
    interpolation (base/mpfr.jl: ccall((string(:mpfr_, f), :libmpfr), ...)),
    and get_sym_or_global_if_const() handled only symbols -- worse, it fell
    off the end of a non-void function for everything else, so the result
    was undefined rather than NULL. Interning a String target makes those
    calls work; the missing return makes the failure reportable.

  * the variadic printf family. The generator emitted calls with the fixed
    arguments only, so mpfr_snprintf(buf, 0, "%Re", x) reached MPFR without
    the value to print and tripped an assertion inside get_str.c. The
    variadic arguments are now forwarded.

  * entries that the generator never saw, because they are not declared in
    julia.h (jl_load_, which is what include() calls) or were added to Base
    later: jl_macroexpand, jl_macroexpand1, jl_get_field_offset,
    jl_typemax_uint, jl_crc32c, jl_lookup_code_address,
    jl_backtrace_from_here, jl_getpid, jl_prepend_cwd,
    jl_type_intersection_with_env, memrchr, jl_get_excstack, and the libm
    functions log2/log10/exp2/expm1/remainder/modf (plus their float
    variants), which Base reaches through its openlibm ccalls.

  * a usable diagnostic: the fallthrough printed the target with no context
    and then raised an exception with an empty message.

Also drop the jl_(e) debug dump at the top of jl_throw(), which printed
every exception -- including caught ones -- to stderr.
